# Dynamic Renderer main-plot pan / bilateral Y axis

## Pre-work plan

- Context: Daedilus direct message `msg-fsi-093703d2c54f410cb67052bd27858870`; Research consumer is on Dynamic Renderer 0.2.30.
- Goal: every TA row exposes readable left/right Y coordinates; main-plot horizontal drag pans by the actual crossed K-bar count without becoming a navigator resize/page gesture.
- Confirmed facts:
  - `RendererModel.mainPlotPanDelta` already maps CSS movement to visible-bar delta.
  - `Renderer.dispatchAdjacentCoverageNow` discards that delta when crossing local coverage and calls `tryAdjacentCoverageIntent`, whose target is `currentStart +/- visibleCount`.
  - The row SVG draws five horizontal grid lines but no Y coordinate labels.
- Invariants:
  - main-plot pan preserves visible `Count` and navigator resize/move behavior;
  - boundary requests use the exact clamped global start implied by the drag delta;
  - both Y axes derive from the same low/high bounds and grid positions used by row geometry;
  - Research source, base-series/1K lifecycle, port 18884, and deployment remain Daedilus-owned.
- Scope: Renderer model/view plus focused Renderer tests; package/version consumers only after source tests pass. Existing unrelated dirty paths remain untouched.
- Intended release: Renderer and Interactive.Client 0.2.31, local package handoff only unless separately authorized.
- Acceptance: source regression demonstrates exact-delta boundary intent/count preservation and bilateral five-tick axis contract; Release package builds and package-backed test projects pass; Daedilus performs Research/18884 focused acceptance.
- Stop condition: deliver package hashes/source commit and focused seam, then return to foreground COMM wait after pending handoff is drained.

